;; rules/booklogic/remedies.edn — proposed actions when a claim is refuted.
;;
;; FORM SYNTAX:
;;   (defremedy :W001-name
;;     :when CONDITION
;;     :propose ACTION
;;     :requires :auto-apply OR :human-review)
;;
;; Remedies are consumed by external workflow code (book-qa) when the
;; verifier reports a refutation. They are NOT executed inside the
;; verifier itself — defremedy forms compile to declarative entries
;; that the QA harness reads. See references/phase-boundaries.md.
;;
;; EXAMPLE (commented out — uncomment and edit for your domain):
;; (defremedy :W001-unsat-core-to-refutation
;;   :when    (unsat-core-contains ?claim)
;;   :propose (ledger/transition ?claim :refuted)
;;   :requires :human-review)
;;
;; COMMON SILENT FAILURES:
;;   - :requires omitted → defaults to :auto-apply. Confirm this is what
;;     you want for the action — auto-applying ledger transitions on every
;;     refutation can cascade quickly. Prefer :human-review for any
;;     remedy that mutates the ledger.
;;   - Remedies are not consumed inside the verifier — they're an
;;     external-consumer contract. Pure defremedy forms don't make the
;;     verifier verdict change.
;;
{:forms []}
